{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":4,"prev":"b9b34e2ff94bcfb3e4ed77f05234db8a161afb3fa0d5cd12b241b7c95175f802","at":"2026-09-27T04:02:01.02996Z","type":"node_output","state":"discover","iter":0,"node":"discover","origin":{"run_id":"mrv-20260927-035959181844000-fsm-sdlc-loop-clean-sdlc-loop-clean-bd2d3192","seq":4,"version":1,"hash":"7127af560990c5015371bd417178a6b5a15067c78162a6e3b53ce80941feb45c"},"data":{"output":{"findings":[{"tag":"advisory","file":"internal/repo/worktree.go","start_line":14,"end_line":18,"issue":"The doc comment declares MainWorktreeFromPorcelain/RunStoreRoot 'the ONE definition of where FSM runs live', but internal/status/fsmruns.go (DiscoverAbandonedRuns, called from status.go:221 with the current-worktree root) still reads <current worktree>/.metareview/runs, so a third reader of the run store was not moved onto the shared seam.","consequence":"From a linked worktree, `metareview status` (and the Stop hook built on it) still cannot see abandoned FSM runs the FSM wrote to the main worktree. This is the same writer/reader split as #169 on a different surface, and the comment tells future maintainers the split cannot happen.","confidence":60,"severity":"P3"},{"tag":"advisory","file":"internal/repo/worktree.go","start_line":31,"end_line":39,"issue":"runStoreGit hardcodes its own 20s timeout and exec path when the repo already has gitcontext.Deadline, the shared git deadline that tests can override. Two git runners now resolve the main worktree: the FSM's c.git runner and this one.","consequence":"If gitcontext.Deadline is tuned or overridden in tests, this call does not follow it. The FSM (writer) and record-lenses (reader) also reach git through different runners, so they can behave differently on timeout or error even though they parse the same porcelain output.","confidence":45,"severity":"P3"}]}}}
