{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":6,"prev":"4a3cb49a387c04cc341f9059ed45cd66c765a3c880676d5881677fe8443b8566","at":"2026-09-27T04:02:01.551688Z","type":"delta_applied","state":"discover","iter":0,"node":"discover","origin":{"run_id":"mrv-20260927-035959181844000-fsm-sdlc-loop-clean-sdlc-loop-clean-bd2d3192","seq":6,"version":1,"hash":"794ec6bf9d99849b7fbf25eb01e3a3090db6f4d4d0bcdd69fd49cbfd635c84f8"},"data":{"findings":[{"issue_text":"[ADVISORY] The doc comment declares MainWorktreeFromPorcelain/RunStoreRoot 'the ONE definition of where FSM runs live', but internal/status/fsmruns.go (DiscoverAbandonedRuns, called from status.go:221 with the current-worktree root) still reads <current worktree>/.metareview/runs, so a third reader of the run store was not moved onto the shared seam. From a linked worktree, `metareview status` (and the Stop hook built on it) still cannot see abandoned FSM runs the FSM wrote to the main worktree. This is the same writer/reader split as #169 on a different surface, and the comment tells future maintainers the split cannot happen.","file":"internal/repo/worktree.go","line":14,"severity":"p3","category":"advisory","source":"lens"}],"output_hash":"4428fb543ca72a7db4e1596ca37cc9ed6b299f97ef94a379b41658feee6a58a3"}}
