{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":50,"prev":"23f41fb8c806a2472096743e6a9670bd565a19db503f9c7efe34ed4b6e2301b7","at":"2026-09-27T04:12:51.749598Z","type":"node_output","state":"recheck","iter":1,"node":"recheck","data":{"output":{"findings":[{"tag":"advisory","file":"internal/repo/worktree.go","start_line":3,"end_line":10,"issue":"internal/repo was a stdlib-only leaf used for root detection by about 11 packages, and it now imports internal/fsm/gate just to reach RealExec's GIT_* scrubbing. That pulls fsm/gate, fsm/run, fsm/converge, fsm/errs, state and jsonl into every importer of repo, and makes the root-detection package and the FSM depend on each other through gate.","consequence":"No import cycle exists today. But fsm/run, fsm/gate, state and jsonl can now never import internal/repo without creating one, and every package that uses repo.Root picks up the FSM execution stack. Moving the hardened git exec into a small leaf package that both gate and repo import would avoid this.","confidence":70,"severity":"P3"},{"tag":"advisory","file":"CHANGELOG.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3,"issue":"The 0.13.4 entry is dated 2026-09-27, but the release commits are dated 2026-09-26 (-0700), and the previous entry used the local commit date.","consequence":"The CHANGELOG release date is one day off from the actual release date.","confidence":45,"severity":"P3"}]}}}
