{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":52,"prev":"49f195733f484f6725282acf92deece8bab5728045acbdcfaf2916cad88d397a","at":"2026-09-27T04:12:52.223219Z","type":"delta_applied","state":"recheck","iter":1,"node":"recheck","data":{"findings":[{"issue_text":"[ADVISORY] internal/repo was a stdlib-only leaf used for root detection by about 11 packages, and it now imports internal/fsm/gate just to reach RealExec's GIT_* scrubbing. That pulls fsm/gate, fsm/run, fsm/converge, fsm/errs, state and jsonl into every importer of repo, and makes the root-detection package and the FSM depend on each other through gate. No import cycle exists today. But fsm/run, fsm/gate, state and jsonl can now never import internal/repo without creating one, and every package that uses repo.Root picks up the FSM execution stack. Moving the hardened git exec into a small leaf package that both gate and repo import would avoid this.","file":"internal/repo/worktree.go","line":3,"severity":"p3","category":"advisory","source":"lens"}],"output_hash":"a4e4fd760ac18f715e382f9cbb3334a30398227a77448786ad096fe0d231914d"}}
