{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":65,"prev":"78a1df608c8a4825394f7d51906e80f287fe108d54f59a383d6143a37758ef41","at":"2026-09-27T04:13:13.091463Z","type":"node_output","state":"adjudicate","iter":2,"node":"adjudicate","data":{"output":{"confirmed":[],"rejected":[{"id":"6aaa792ebb5e","desc":"[ADVISORY] internal/repo was a stdlib-only leaf used for root detection by about 11 packages, and it now imports internal/fsm/gate just to reach RealExec's GIT_* scrubbing. That pulls fsm/gate, fsm/run, fsm/converge, fsm/errs, state and jsonl into every importer of repo, and makes the root-detection package and the FSM depend on each other through gate. No import cycle exists today. But fsm/run, fsm/gate, state and jsonl can now never import internal/repo without creating one, and every package that uses repo.Root picks up the FSM execution stack. Moving the hardened git exec into a small leaf package that both gate and repo import would avoid this.","file":"internal/repo/worktree.go","line":3,"verdict":"hallucination","confidence":0.94}]}}}
